{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Group C was one of four groups of national teams competing in the second stage of the [[1982 FIFA World Cup]]. The group's three matches were staged at the [[Estadi de Sarrià|Estadio Sarriá]] in [[Barcelona]]. The group consisted of three teams advancing from the first group stage: Group 1 runners-up [[Italy national football team|Italy]], Group 6 winners [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] and the Group 3 runners-up, the reigning world champions [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/82full.html |title=World Cup 1982 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

Italy topped the group and advanced to the semi-finals, eventually winning the competition.

In 2007, ''[[The Guardian]]'' called this group the deadliest-ever [[Group of Death]] in FIFA World Cup history.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2007/dec/12/theknowledge.sport |title=The Knowledge: the deadliest group of death ever |first=John |last=Ashdown |author2=Alan Gardner |author3=James Dart |work=The Guardian |date=12 December 2007 |accessdate=17 June 2018 }}</ref>

==Qualified teams==
The winner of Group 6 and the runners-up of Group 1 and 3 qualified for Group C of the second round.

